Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 05:05:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix exam preset collision bugs, wire up preset picker UI, add
 Custom mode

Found EXAM_PRESETS/applyExamPreset() already added to the repo (JEE/NEET/CA/
UPSC with real syllabus data) but not wired up and had its own version of the
subject-collision bug:

- Boot init and QR-import merge both iterated ALL of ALL_SYLLABI (every
  subject from every exam) regardless of which preset was active, so
  switching exams didn't actually stop subjects from bleeding together
- saveSyllabus() rebuilt S.subjects from the ENTIRE S.customSyllabi history
  (every subject ever edited across every preset you've used), so editing
  a topic in your current exam could resurrect a previous exam's subjects
- switchEditSubject/saveSyllabus both re-read the DOM picker as source of
  truth independently, which could drift out of sync with each other

Fixed by adding rebuildSubjects() as the single source of truth for
S.subjects (always scoped to S.examPreset), used everywhere subjects get
rebuilt, and tracking _activeEditSubject explicitly instead of re-deriving
it from the DOM each time.

Also: added CUSTOM preset (blank, build your own), wired up the picker UI
(nav item + page, two-tap confirm since switching is destructive to the
subject list), onboarding auto-nav to the picker on fresh installs, and
included examPreset in the QR sync payload so both devices stay aligned.
